.* WRKBNDDIR: the binding directories with their options. The first
.* entry is blank: option 1 on it creates a directory.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Quartz Systems 2026
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TEXTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 50'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=BNDDIR CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=BNDLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=BNDTEXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=DIRS VARS='OPT BNDDIR BNDLIB BNDTEXT'.
:KEYL NAME=KEYS HELP=KEYSHLP.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.F11=Display names only
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='RETURN 16'.F16=Repeat position to
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION='RETURN 17'.F17=Position to
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKBNDDIR KEYL=KEYS HELP=WRKBNDDH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SPACE.Work with Binding Directories
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=DIRS VIEWS=2 SCROLL=YES EXTACT=YES.
:LISTACT HELP='WRKBNDDIR/OPTIONS' OPTION=1 ACTFOR=EXTACT ENTER='RETURN 1'.1=Create
:LISTACT HELP='WRKBNDDIR/OPTIONS' OPTION=4 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 4'.4=Delete
:LISTACT HELP='WRKBNDDIR/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD DSPBNDDIR BNDDIR(&BNDLIB./&BNDDIR.)'.5=Display
:LISTACT HELP='WRKBNDDIR/OPTIONS' OPTION=9 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD DSPBNDDIR BNDDIR(&BNDLIB./&BNDDIR.)'.9=Work with binding directory entries
:LISTACT HELP='WRKBNDDIR/OPTIONS' OPTION=13 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?CHGOBJD OBJ(&BNDLIB./&BNDDIR.) OBJTYPE(*BNDDIR)'.13=Change description
:LISTCOL HELP='WRKBNDDIR/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/BNDDIR' VAR=BNDDIR USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES.Binding Directory
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/BNDLIB' VAR=BNDLIB USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES.Library
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/BNDTEXT' VAR=BNDTEXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Text
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT BNDDIR BNDLIB BNDTEXT'.
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT BNDDIR BNDLIB'.
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 1, 5 and 13 or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKBNDDH.Work with Binding Directories - Help
:P.The binding directories the name selects. Type 1 on the blank
first line to create one, 4 to delete one, 5 or 9 to see its entries,
13 to change its text.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=KEYSHLP.Function keys - Help
:P.F3 leaves the display, F12 goes back one display, F5 reads the
directories again.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='WRKBNDDIR/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/BNDDIR'.Binding Directory
:P.The binding directories the binder searches for modules and service
programs to resolve imports.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/BNDLIB'.Library
:P.The library of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/BNDTEXT'.Text
:P.The text of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKBNDDIR/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Create
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to create it.
:PT.4=Delete
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to delete it.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it. The Display
Binding Directory (DSPBNDDIR) command runs for the entry.
:PT.9=Work with binding directory entries
:PD.Type 9 next to an entry and press Enter to work with binding
directory entries it. The Display Binding Directory (DSPBNDDIR) command
runs for the entry.
:PT.13=Change description
:PD.Type 13 next to an entry and press Enter to change description it.
The Change Object Description (CHGOBJD) command is prompted for the
entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
